## Development

When starting the dev server, use background mode:

```
astro dev --background
```

Manage the background server with `astro dev stop`, `astro dev status`, and
`astro dev logs`.

## Build & asset wiring

This site is a curated, human-readable companion to the repo's
<%= it.displayName %> reverse-engineering notes. Three things are
**generated**, never edited by hand:

- `public/assets/<%= it.game %>/` — copied from the repo's
  `public/assets/<%= it.game %>` by `scripts/build.mjs`, so the site is
  self-contained. When the source is missing (e.g. in CI, which never has
  the original copyrighted game files), the already-committed copy under
  this site's own `public/assets/<%= it.game %>` is used instead — that
  committed copy only exists because a previous local build produced it, so
  it must stay committed even though the repo-root extraction output usually
  isn't.
- `public/favicon.png` — either the placeholder this scaffold ships with, or
  generated by `scripts/generate_favicon.mjs` from a real sprite frame once
  `scripts/build.mjs`'s `FAVICON_FRAME`/`FAVICON_ATLAS_DIR`/`FAVICON_MANIFEST`
  constants are pointed at one (see README.md).
- `generated/sidebar.mjs` — the Starlight sidebar, generated from
  `src/content/docs/<%= it.game %>/_sidebar.json`.

`npm run dev` and `npm run build` run `scripts/build.mjs` first, so assets,
favicon and the sidebar stay in sync automatically. Run it manually with
`node scripts/build.mjs`.

### Editing the site

This section covers **wiring** — where things live and what regenerates what.
For **content standards** — the page types and their skeletons, how claims must
be evidenced, gallery patterns, and the pre-publish checklist — read
`WRITING-GUIDE.md`. (Agent sessions: the account-wide `seer-website` skill
carries the same standard in more depth, with per-page-type playbooks and an
audit mode.)

- **Curated pages** live in `src/content/docs/<%= it.game %>/`. If this
  project also keeps raw research notes elsewhere in the repo (e.g.
  `docs/<%= it.game %>/`), curated pages should summarise that research —
  when a curated page disagrees with the raw notes, the raw notes win. Update
  the curated page, not the other way around.
- **Sidebar order/labels**: edit
  `src/content/docs/<%= it.game %>/_sidebar.json`, then re-run the build
  script. Slugs are the content file paths under `src/content/docs/` (the
  game's home page slug is `<%= it.game %>`, not `<%= it.game %>/index`).
- **Sprite galleries**: use `src/components/SpriteGallery.astro`, passing
  `manifest`/`assetPath` for the packed-frames atlas to render, and
  optionally `hoverPairs`/`clickChains`/`labels` for hover-swap, click-cycle,
  and display-name behavior. The component has no built-in knowledge of any
  game's data shapes — the calling page builds the `labels` map itself from
  whatever name data actually exists. See README.md for a worked example.
- **Images**: use a raw `<img src="...">` tag (never markdown `![]()` syntax —
  see the base-path note below) with a **relative** path to the copied asset,
  e.g. `<img src="../../assets/<%= it.game %>/amiga/screens/title.png">` from
  a page two directories deep. Re-run the build script after the repo's
  `public/assets` changes.

### Asset-resync workflow

When the upstream extraction changes (new sprites, corrected data, etc.):

1. Regenerate the extraction locally so the repo's `public/assets/<%= it.game %>`
   is current.
2. Run `npm run dev` or `npm run build` in this site — `scripts/build.mjs`
   re-copies the assets and regenerates the sidebar/favicon as needed.
3. Commit whatever changed under this site's `public/assets/<%= it.game %>`
   (and `public/favicon.png`, if it changed) — that's the mirror CI deploys
   from.

## If this site deploys under a subpath (`base` is set in `astro.config.mjs`)

Most seer sites get their own subdomain and deploy at a domain root, where
none of this matters. If `astro.config.mjs` has a non-empty `base` (e.g.
GitHub Pages project pages, `base: '/my-repo'`), be aware: Astro/Starlight do
**not** auto-prefix hand-authored links or images with it — not even inside
Starlight's own frontmatter fields (e.g. a splash page's
`hero.actions[].link`). Starlight's own *generated* chrome (sidebar,
pagination, breadcrumbs, favicon) is base-aware automatically; anything you
typed a path into yourself, YAML or JS, is not.

This scaffold already writes every link and image the safe way — **keep
following the same pattern**:

- In `.astro` components or `.mdx` frontmatter/JS, build paths with
  `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, but normalize its trailing slash first — it is
  **not** guaranteed to end in `/` (that depends on the separate
  `trailingSlash` config, not on how `base` is written):
  `` const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, ''); `${base}/assets/...` ``.
- In markdown/MDX prose *and* frontmatter YAML link fields, use a
  **relative path**, not an absolute `/<%= it.game %>/...` or `/assets/...` —
  e.g. `../graphics/` for a sibling page, `../../assets/<%= it.game
  %>/amiga/foo.png` for an image two directories deep, or just
  `<%= it.game %>/`/`assets/foo.png` with no prefix from the depth-0
  homepage. Never hardcode the deployed base path itself.
- **Never use markdown `![alt](path)` image syntax for a `public/assets/`
  image.** Astro's markdown pipeline intercepts that syntax specifically: an
  absolute path silently skips base-prefixing, and a relative path fails the
  build outright (`[ImageNotFound]`, since it tries to import it as a local
  `src/`-relative asset). A raw `<img src="...">` HTML tag has neither
  problem — it passes through untouched in both `.md` and `.mdx`.

Full writeup with the empirical evidence behind this:
`~/.claude/skills/seer-website/references/base-path.md` (if using the
account-wide `seer-website` skill). Before calling any subpath-deploy change
done, build with the real `base` set and grep `dist/**/*.html` (including the
homepage) for un-prefixed `href="/`/`src="/`.

